-- Status: UNVERIFIED
MODULE [adv_clean]
THEOREM [adv_clean]:
  GIVEN:
    - [hx]: $x$ is a real number
  CLAIM:
    $x^2 \geq 0$
PROOF OF [adv_clean]:
  [1] CASE $x \geq 0$:
    [1.1] HAVE $x \cdot x \geq 0$.
          BY [1.0], the product of two nonnegatives is nonnegative.
    [1] QED BY [1.1].
  [2] CASE $x < 0$:
    [2.1] HAVE $-x > 0$.
          BY [2.0], negating a negative gives a positive.
    [2.2] HAVE $x \cdot x = (-x) \cdot (-x) \geq 0$.
          BY [2.1], the product of two positives is positive.
    [2] QED BY [2.2].
  [3] SHOW $x^2 \geq 0$.
      BY [1], [2], the cases are exhaustive.
  QED BY [3].
